From 1eb9ceec149990be25017a4ccb75343ad41ee279 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrice Chotard <patrice.chotard@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Apr 2026 15:41:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: stm32: add ethernet_mac_address on stm32mp15

Describe MAC address cells available in bsec data register.
It is useful to read the OTP value with NVMEM if the MAC address
is not provided in the device tree by the BootLoader.

Change-Id: I022dad943f60be3716448a70532b5109f358000b
Signed-off-by: Christophe Roullier <christophe.roullier@st.com>
Signed-off-by: Patrice Chotard <patrice.chotard@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/557487
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Amelie DELAUNAY <amelie.delaunay@foss.st.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/st/stm32mp151.dtsi | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/st/stm32mp151.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/st/stm32mp151.dtsi
@@ -783,6 +783,9 @@
 			ts_cal2: calib@5e {
 				reg = <0x5e 0x2>;
 			};
+			ethernet_mac_address: mac@e4 {
+				reg = <0xe4 0x6>;
+			};
 		};
 
 		etzpc: bus@5c007000 {
